CONCEPT: A Downs cell uses molten NaCl, separated electrode compartments, and continuous product outlets to reduce Na+ to liquid sodium at the cathode while oxidizing Cl− to Cl2 gas at the anode without letting the products recombine.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): The Downs cell works because molten salt supplies Na+ and Cl− without water, and the iron screen plus separate outlets keep newly formed sodium metal and chlorine gas apart.
DEMO STEPS: 4 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

